Additionally, we paid additional principal each month on our mortgage for the past three years or so. Once we challenged SPS, they removed our ability to pay extra monthly principal with our monthly payments. The box on their website to pay additional principal was removed and it had always been there every month. I spoke to an SPS agent on the phone about this and he stated Ive never seen this happen unless a mortgage was not being paid on time. Youve never been late, so I do not understand. With that, we can only assume this is further retaliation by SPS for challenging them over the additional {$18000.00}.

I had been speaking with an SPS agent by the name of XXXX who seemed to want to help us get answers to our questions. XXXX made a statement on the phone the last time I spoke with him that he had heard of unethical business practices by XXXX XXXX XXXX. XXXX gave me his direct extension, but oddly enough, he never returned any future calls when I left messages, and I was not granted the opportunity to speak with XXXX again even after asking for him many times. I can only assume SPS prevented him from speaking further with us, but Im sure they will deny that and I can not prove it. If SPS records their calls as they say they do, my comments can be validated. 

I truly have zero recollection of verbally agreeing to defer over {$18000.00} of principal and my wife has never spoken to anyone about our mortgage, and she is the primary signature. Neither of us have ever signed anything relating to deferred interest. That amount would be more than 14 monthly payments. If that were true, I see no way we would be in our home.

